  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let us assume&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is connected balanced wheat stone bridge, such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> as shown below,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/41a068b4-0b7a-4dec-b0d0-aeada99a2def-image.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 199px;\" />&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />If galvanometer and cell is exchanged, then circuit becomes as shown in below figure,&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/620fa190-d812-4e10-bfd9-9652fbf2c15f-image.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 187px;\" /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br /><br />The circuit is redrawn and can be visualised as below figure,&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c433b183-fc93-496d-924b-98debda54f30-image.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 156px;\" /><br /><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<br />In this case, if it is balanced, then there must be,&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math><br /><br />Equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;realises that, both equations are same, which means null point is not affected.</p>",
